---
name: reflection
description: >
  A persona's own successful action, recorded as a first-person observation
  memory (backend/smallville_agents.py, remember_outcome). The command verb
  selects the phrasing: arriving somewhere, doing an activity, or a quoted
  fallback for any other command. The memory's importance is chosen in Python
  (it is data, not text), so only the wording lives here.
inputs:
  verb:
    type: string
    description: The command verb -- "travel", "perform", or anything else.
  location:
    type: string
    description: The place arrived at (used when verb == "travel").
  activity:
    type: string
    description: What the persona is doing (used when verb == "perform").
  command:
    type: string
    description: The raw command, quoted verbatim in the fallback (any other verb).
sample:
  verb: travel
  location: Hobbs Cafe
  activity: ""
  command: ""
---
{%- if verb == "travel" -%}
I traveled to {{ location }}.
{%- elif verb == "perform" -%}
I am {{ activity }}.
{%- else -%}
I did "{{ command }}".
{%- endif -%}
